    {
      "section": "story.manifesto",
      "variant": "default",
      "content": {
        "headingLines": [
          "Software",
          "doesn't",
          "close deals.",
          "You do."
        ],
        "paragraphs": [
          "So it's strange that sales teams revolve around CRMs that were never built for you. They were built for storing things. And no matter how well organized or how fully automated, storage rooms were never the point.",
          "We think you deserve a proper place to work. Call it a workshop, a studio, a lab, a kitchen. Wherever you do your best work. Same materials, same tools, but intentionally prepared and arranged. Everything exactly where your hand expects it.",
          "A place like that remembers what you can't, surfaces what matters, keeps you on pace.",
          "The relationships, the judgment calls, the close — that part has always been yours. We just built a better place to do it."
        ],
        "emphasisPhrase": "a proper place to work.",
        "signature": {
          "team": "Team Operate",
          "date": "09.30.26"
        },
        "ticket": {
          "brand": "OPERATE",
          "version": "2.0",
          "subjectLabel": "Subject",
          "subject": "A PROPER PLACE TO WORK",
          "fields": [
            {
              "term": "Date",
              "value": "2026"
            },
            {
              "term": "Vol.",
              "value": "1"
            },
            {
              "term": "Ref.",
              "value": "B001"
            }
          ]
        },
